{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES REQUESTED on exact clean pushed head b91d6a7283ced2525be41196f32edc10d3634d75 / internal/gitstore artifact 07acd616.\n\nArchitecture: the change stays wholly in layer 1, Ordinary Git storage (`internal/gitstore`). It preserves the documented adapter contract that failed or untrustworthy Git questions return errors rather than negative or partial answers, so docs/reference/architecture.md needs no update. The fixed-stride parser and one batched raw-object check are in the right layer.\n\nSecurity: the raw `hash-object --literally` NUL regression now closes the reproduced silent-body-truncation case, but the batched validator is not fail closed. `git cat-file --batch` writes `\u003coid\u003e missing` to stdout and exits 0 for a missing object. `refuseMalformedCommits` only searches the combined output for NUL, so a disappearance, corruption, or race between `git log` and `cat-file` returns success and exposes rows whose raw commit was never validated. Parse the batch protocol: require exactly one response for every requested hash, the matching OID, type `commit`, a valid bounded size, the exact payload and terminator; reject missing, malformed, extra and truncated responses; scan each exact payload for NUL. Add load-bearing parser/refusal cases, including the successful-exit `missing` response. The ref-name test also overclaims: the `\\x00` argv case is rejected by Go/exec before Git runs, while `\\x1f`, `\\x1e`, and `\\x07` really reach Git and are refused. Separate the OS/filesystem NUL invariant from Git ref validation rather than attributing all four to Git.\n\nSimplification: keep the single fixed-stride log parser and one batched `cat-file` subprocess. A small size-framed batch-response parser with exact-count checks is simpler and safer than a global byte scan or invoking `fsck`; no second graph delimiter protocol and no per-commit subprocess are needed.\n\nVerified at the exact head: canonical Rests-On child cbf40740, clean worktree matching origin, main b7f5b015 ancestor, `git diff main...HEAD --check`, `go test -count=1 ./internal/gitstore`, and `go vet ./internal/gitstore` pass. A direct all-zero OID probe produces `missing` with exit 0, proving the blocking path; 50 scans of an 81-commit repository took about 0.81 seconds, so batching remains proportionate. Ordinary reasoning staleness is acknowledged; neither the artifact nor review describes a different commit.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:07acd616889bc70c62e87840e77cc30d6c00a42f","head":"b91d6a7283ced2525be41196f32edc10d3634d75","verdict":"changes-requested"}}